advanced-health-surgery-needs-operator = Another operator is required for surgery.
advanced-health-procedure-started = Prepared. Procedure in progress — stay beside the patient.
advanced-health-surgical-open = Open surgical access
advanced-health-surgical-open-desc = Control internal bleeding and unstable fractures, then close the access with a surgical closure kit.
advanced-health-surgical-prepared = Site prepared
advanced-health-surgical-prepared-desc = The wounds are clean. Deep procedures require active regional anesthesia.
advanced-health-local-anesthesia = Regional anesthesia active
advanced-health-local-anesthesia-desc = Pain in this region is temporarily suppressed. Consciousness and tissue injuries remain; pain may return when it wears off.
advanced-health-bone-fixed = Fracture fixed
advanced-health-bone-fixed-desc = Fixation supports function while the bone heals. Close the access and maintain circulation; an applied tourniquet prevents recovery.
ent-AdvancedWoundIrrigationKit = sterile wound irrigation kit
    .desc = Cleans wounds and prepares a surgical site. Does not cure an established infection.
ent-AdvancedRegionalAnesthetic = regional anesthetic kit
    .desc = Provides temporary regional pain control without putting the patient to sleep.
ent-AdvancedBoneFixationKit = bone fixation kit
    .desc = Stabilises a fracture through an open surgical access. The bone still needs time to heal.
ent-AdvancedSurgicalClosureKit = surgical closure kit
    .desc = Closes a prepared surgical access after bleeding and unstable fractures have been treated.
ent-AdvancedTraumaShears = trauma shears
    .desc = Releases an applied tourniquet. Uncontrolled bleeding can resume immediately.
